        "id": "ch2_4-1",
        "text": "Working with files and directories\nRemember that everything in Linux is a file. A directory is a file too. As such, it is essential to know\nhow to work with them. Working with files in Linux implies the use of several commands for basic file\nand directory operations, file viewing, file creation, file location, file properties, and linking. Some of\nthe commands, which will not be covered here, have uses closely related to files. These will be covered\nin the following section.\nEsta secci\u00f3n contiene las siguientes subsecciones\n\u2022 Understanding file paths\n\u2022 Basic file operations\n\u2022 Commands for file viewing\n\u2022 Commands for file properties\nSi deseas explorar cualquiera de estas subsecciones, puedes pregunt\u00e1rmelo directamente.",
